      "message": "This should be in `zephyr/shim/core/riscv/`, since it\u0027s something supported by the RISC-V architecture, not just this specific chip.\n\nMight make sense to call it `mpu.c` to mirror the [cortex-m version](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c;l\u003d144-159;drc\u003db088e3950aa69eca808f585917220ea0b576531c). Although this uses PMP, the function is called `mpu_lock_rollback`, so I think it makes sense. In a future CL, we may want to rename \"mpu_lock_rollback\" to something more generic that applies to both ARM\u0027s MPU and RISC-V\u0027s PMP.",
